{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:lorentz-metric-of-rank-one-distribution","title":"prop:lorentz-metric-of-rank-one-distribution","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":3090,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:lorentz-metric-of-rank-one-distribution","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:lorentz-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:rank-one-distribution]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existence-riemannian-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:lorentz-form-pointwise]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:sign-flipped-form]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:sign-flipped-form-smooth]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:two-unit-vectors-of-a-line]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:local-unit-section]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:lorentz-metric-of-rank-one-distribution","line":5335,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Sufficiency in Theorem \\ref{thm:lorentz-metrics}]\n\\label{prop:lorentz-metric-of-rank-one-distribution}\n\n\\uses{def:lorentz-metric, def:rank-one-distribution, prop:existence-riemannian-metric, lem:lorentz-form-pointwise}\n\n\n\n\nIf $M$ admits a rank-1 tangent distribution, then it admits a Lorentz metric.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:lorentz-form-pointwise,prop:existence-riemannian-metric,def:sign-flipped-form,lem:sign-flipped-form-smooth,lem:two-unit-vectors-of-a-line,lem:local-unit-section}\n\\sketch Choose a Riemannian metric $g$. For each $x$, choose either unit vector\n$u_x$ in the line $D_x$ and set\n\\[\n\\bar g_x(v,w)=g_x(v,w)-2g_x(v,u_x)g_x(w,u_x).\n\\]\nThe pointwise sign-flip lemma makes this independent of the choice $u_x$ and gives\nsignature $(n,1)$ when $\\dim M=n+1$. Locally choose a smooth unit section $E$ of\n$D$. Since $E_x=\\pm u_x$, the field $\\bar g$ equals the smooth field\n$\\flip(g,E)$ locally; hence $\\bar g$ is a Lorentz metric.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Sufficiency in Theorem <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23thm%3Alorentz-metrics\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:lorentz-metrics\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a6c6f72656e747a2d6d657472696373\">4</a>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a6c6f72656e747a2d6d65747269632d6f662d72616e6b2d6f6e652d646973747269627574696f6e\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Alorentz-metric\">↗ def:lorentz-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Arank-one-distribution\">↗ def:rank-one-distribution</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aexistence-riemannian-metric\">↗ prop:existence-riemannian-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Alorentz-form-pointwise\">↗ lem:lorentz-form-pointwise</a> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> admits a rank-1 tangent distribution, then it admits a Lorentz metric.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Alorentz-form-pointwise\">↗ lem:lorentz-form-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aexistence-riemannian-metric\">↗ prop:existence-riemannian-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asign-flipped-form\">↗ def:sign-flipped-form</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asign-flipped-form-smooth\">↗ lem:sign-flipped-form-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Atwo-unit-vectors-of-a-line\">↗ lem:two-unit-vectors-of-a-line</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Alocal-unit-section\">↗ lem:local-unit-section</a> \\sketch Choose a Riemannian metric <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span>. For each <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span>, choose either unit vector <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u_x$\">$u_x$</span> in the line <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$D_x$\">$D_x$</span> and set </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\bar g_x(v,w)=g_x(v,w)-2g_x(v,u_x)g_x(w,u_x).  \\]\">\\[  \\bar g_x(v,w)=g_x(v,w)-2g_x(v,u_x)g_x(w,u_x).  \\]</span></p><p> The pointwise sign-flip lemma makes this independent of the choice <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u_x$\">$u_x$</span> and gives signature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(n,1)$\">$(n,1)$</span> when <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\dim M=n+1$\">$\\dim M=n+1$</span>. Locally choose a smooth unit section <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$E$\">$E$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$D$\">$D$</span>. Since <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$E_x=\\pm u_x$\">$E_x=\\pm u_x$</span>, the field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\bar g$\">$\\bar g$</span> equals the smooth field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\flip (g,E)$\">$\\flip (g,E)$</span> locally; hence <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\bar g$\">$\\bar g$</span> is a Lorentz metric. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:local-unit-section","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:simple-eigenpair","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:lorentz-metric","title":"def:lorentz-metric","label":"def:lorentz-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:rank-one-distribution","title":"def:rank-one-distribution","label":"def:rank-one-distribution"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existence-riemannian-metric","title":"prop:existence-riemannian-metric","label":"prop:existence-riemannian-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:lorentz-form-pointwise","title":"lem:lorentz-form-pointwise","label":"lem:lorentz-form-pointwise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:sign-flipped-form","title":"def:sign-flipped-form","label":"def:sign-flipped-form"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:sign-flipped-form-smooth","title":"lem:sign-flipped-form-smooth","label":"lem:sign-flipped-form-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:two-unit-vectors-of-a-line","title":"lem:two-unit-vectors-of-a-line","label":"lem:two-unit-vectors-of-a-line"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:local-unit-section","title":"lem:local-unit-section","label":"lem:local-unit-section"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:lorentz-metrics","title":"thm:lorentz-metrics","label":"thm:lorentz-metrics"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:lorentz-metric-of-rank-one-distribution","title":"prop:lorentz-metric-of-rank-one-distribution","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[Sufficiency in Theorem \\ref{thm:lorentz-metrics}]\n\\label{prop:lorentz-metric-of-rank-one-distribution}\n\n\\uses{def:lorentz-metric, def:rank-one-distribution, prop:existence-riemannian-metric, lem:lorentz-form-pointwise}\n\n\n\n\nIf $M$ admits a rank-1 tangent distribution, then it admits a Lorentz metric.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:lorentz-form-pointwise,prop:existence-riemannian-metric,def:sign-flipped-form,lem:sign-flipped-form-smooth,lem:two-unit-vectors-of-a-line,lem:local-unit-section}\n\\sketch Choose a Riemannian metric $g$. For each $x$, choose either unit vector\n$u_x$ in the line $D_x$ and set\n\\[\n\\bar g_x(v,w)=g_x(v,w)-2g_x(v,u_x)g_x(w,u_x).\n\\]\nThe pointwise sign-flip lemma makes this independent of the choice $u_x$ and gives\nsignature $(n,1)$ when $\\dim M=n+1$. Locally choose a smooth unit section $E$ of\n$D$. Since $E_x=\\pm u_x$, the field $\\bar g$ equals the smooth field\n$\\flip(g,E)$ locally; hence $\\bar g$ is a Lorentz metric.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:lorentz-metric","title":"def:lorentz-metric","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprin